WEBVTT

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:57.630
Sorry, but they suddenly asked me to help out at the store, so I can't go.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.180
Go on ahead by yourself.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:01.680
Takahashi.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.470
Yeah?

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.640
Wanna go somewhere today?

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.560
U-Umm... I was going to an all-you-can-eat cake buffet with Mizu-chin and Taka-chan.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.730
Ah... I see.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:21.740
She's broke whenever she's with me, and she hates having me pay for her, so she only asks for fruit milk...

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.950
Yano!

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.080
Weren't you guys going to an all-you-can-eat cake place or something?

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.620
All-you-can-eat cake?

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.540
Ah, yeah, we went last week.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.170
Nana couldn't go, because she didn't have any money or something.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.590
She was pretty green with envy, so why don't you go with her sometime?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:45.140
Yano, where are you headed? I couldn't get Takeuchi.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.220
Don't follow me.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.980
W-What are you doing?

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.310
Can't you tell?

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.230
I'm in the middle of...

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.820
...stalking my girlfriend.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.320
Huh? For a Christmas present?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:03.320
Yeah, I thought you'd know what Yano likes, Takeuchi-kun, so I was hoping we could go shopping for a bit.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.040
I'm sure he'd be happy with anything you picked out yourself, Takahashi.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.330
Don't say that!

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.410
Please!

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.210
Takeuchi-kun?

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.840
What? You can't make it? Why not?

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:26.600
I really think Yano will like something you pick out yourself a lot more.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.270
But I have no sense for those things...

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.350
Think about it this way. If Yano got you a present...

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:36.980
...would you prefer something your friends picked out for him that they knew you'd like...

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.860
...or something you don't really like that he picked out himself after lots of consideration?

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.950
Which would make you happier?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:43.860
Well...

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:49.950
Of course, the one that Yano picked out himself...

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:50.870
See?

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:53.870
She's on the move again.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.130
Ah, she slipped.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.260
What's she doing, really?

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.140
I could ask you the same question.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.640
What? She must be out buying you a present.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.650
Even though you're penniless...

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.650
You big dummy.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.160
So what's going on with Takeuchi?

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.290
Ah, he said he had to help out at the store, so he couldn't come.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.000
It's the end of the year, so it makes sense.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.120
I see.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.130
I was just overreacting.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.420
Ah, here she comes.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.210
And she has a bag.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.130
All right!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.130
That ends today's stalking!

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.390
I-Idiot! She'll notice us!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.890
I thought you couldn't make it...

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.940
I was worried that you might not've been able to get anything.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.900
But I see you did. I'm glad.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.770
That was it. See you later.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.690
Ah! Since you're out this way, wanna get something to drink?

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.700
Ah, it's okay. That's really all I came for.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.370
It's so tiny...

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.580
I heard from Masa...

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.590
That girl who was in the accident last year... she was your girlfriend at that time?

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.300
I also heard that you haven't even visited her grave yet, either?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.720
You can't do stuff like that.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.430
Why not?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.640
I'm not saying this for your girlfriend's benefit. I'm saying this for yours.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:37.140
Go buy some flowers she liked, some water, and get out there, Motoharu.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.560
People need to cry every now and then--

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.520
I don't want to hear it!

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.980
She was a stupid bitch.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:42.650
Moto!

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.530
Even stupid bitches feel regret.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.450
Even if she does regret it, it's too late!

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.460
Hey, boys! Take this seriously!

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.460
Don't have a snowball fight!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.380
It's so cold!

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.170
Geez! We'll never finish like this!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.970
Yano hasn't looked at me once today.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.970
Is it just my imagination?

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.980
It... isn't my imagination!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.060
Yano!

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.310
Come on!

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.980
What's he so mad about?

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:21.980
Yano!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.410
Takahashi.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.410
Hey, that's stupid. Get up.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.290
Takahashi.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.070
Yano?

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.910
Don't screw around like that.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.370
It was obviously a joke...

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.830
You're so mean...

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.550
I still might not have fully understood Yano at that time...

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.420
Yano!

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.430
Yano!

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.940
There's your Christmas present, you bastard!

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:15.890
I'm sorry...

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.810
I didn't do it out of spite...

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.480
It's okay. Because you're still alive.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.980
It can be really painful at times...

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.740
What could it be?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.910
Umm, I had a really hard time deciding.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.740
Ah, it's a cap.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.160
W-What do you think?

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:42.750
You said you liked hats, and I didn't think you had one with a fuzzy ball on top...

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.830
And I had a really hard time picking the colors...

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.710
...but if you don't like it, they said you could come back and exchange it for another!

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.250
Why would I?

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.340
Don't you think it suits me?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.720
It does!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:58.550
Then it's fine.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.060
Thank you.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.060
Here's mine, too.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.280
I guess I'll be drinking nothing but fruit milk for a while myself.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:20.950
You're crying? Doofus.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.330
It's just that...

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.710
Everything and anything moves you, doesn't it?

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.540
Yeah.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:29.840
People are always telling me to only cry when I'm sad.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:36.090
If you have to cry, then I think tears of happiness are a lot better than tears of sadness.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:45.180
Ever since I met Yano, I've felt that my tears have gotten so much more fragile.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:51.320
Ah! I left my Math book in my locker!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.400
Huh? Let's go back and get it.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.570
It's such a pain...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.110
Don't say that. We were assigned a ton of homework.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.780
Ah, I'm going to the girl's room  for a second, okay?

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:01.620
Yep.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.550
For when I fell down the stairs the other day...

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.550
Thank you.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.970
Y-Yeah.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.140
But don't save me ever again.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:23.470
I don't want to owe you anything.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:29.440
If you hate me that much, we shouldn't have even gotten to know each other to begin with.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:35.480
You only used me to get revenge on my sister, anyway.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.490
"Revenge"?

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.570
That wouldn't mean anything, and I'd have no reason to do that.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.240
Don't go giving everything a hidden meaning.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.460
Then, why did you cry back then?

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:54.460
Why did you cry that time?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.110
Yano!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.990
"Cry"?

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.610
Yano cried?

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.490
Has something like that ever really happened?

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.410
Then, why did you cry back then?

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:31.500
When did this happen?

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.840
And in front of Yamamoto-san...

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:37.420
What could make that happen...?

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:46.100
Sorry for making you listen to my problems again.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.020
And we're on winter break, too...

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:51.390
It's okay. I was wondering what was up.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:55.690
Speaking honestly for a sec, I... can't really believe it.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.110
That he actually cried.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:04.110
I've known him almost my whole life, but I've never seen him cry or show his soft side.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:07.120
Yeah, you told me that before, didn't you?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.870
Well, I guess it's because he's human.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:13.120
Everyone can always do that when nobody else is around...

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:17.630
...but I always thought Yano was different.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:21.630
You can understand, right?

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.130
Yeah.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:30.060
Umm... did something happen between Yamamoto-san and Yano in middle school?

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:33.980
Sometimes, I think there's something strange between them.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:37.060
Not really. Nothing unusual, at least.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.900
Yamamoto was like that back then, too.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.650
If they seem kind of awkward to you, then isn't it just because...

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:44.990
...they're both related to Nana-san in some way?

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:51.160
I wonder why Nana-san was in that car with her ex...

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:55.790
I wonder why she did something like that to betray Yano...

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.840
Was her ex really that charming?

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.500
No way.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.300
He was the worst.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.880
Everyone was always asking why she was going out with a bum like him.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.800
She was always bruised all over.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.470
Bruised?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.020
Why would she stay with someone like him?

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:15.480
People also always asked Yano, "Why are you with someone as stupid as that?"

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.270
That's just what love is.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.070
I guess...

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.160
It's something only those in the relationship could know.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.160
Thanks.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.490
Sorry for calling you out when it's so cold.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.160
Yano and I must really seem like such a stupid couple, too, huh?

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.290
Getting everyone involved like this and working ourselves up over every little thing.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:41.380
Not at all. I think any couple that isn't stupid isn't a real couple anyway.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.970
Takeuchi-kun, when those two first started going out...

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:50.390
...did you also think "why was he going out with someone so stupid?"

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:52.060
Yeah.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:58.400
It pissed me off... they were so dumb and stupid that I couldn't take my eyes off them.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.980
Ever since the beginning.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.580
I'm in the front again!

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.580
I have no luck with getting seats!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.580
Hey, look.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.840
Geez...

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:27.380
Talk about the worst possible combination.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.840
That seating change was the worst.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.260
I won't be able to leave anything behind now.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.890
Ah, when you forget your textbook, you can ask me for mine.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.890
The person next to me will let me share.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.400
Thanks. And when I start nodding off and it seems like I'm gonna be called on, poke me, okay?

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.690
That's a little impossible.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.230
Ah... this will be the second time I'll be sitting next to Yamamoto.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.490
The second time since my second year of middle school.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:51.070
Really? She didn't share her textbooks then, either?

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:56.200
Ah, yeah. Or... maybe not. I don't think I ever forgot them back then.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:58.830
What is it?

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.380
No... it's nothing.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:12.550
I'm no good. When I think Nana-san's involved, I can't help getting weak in the knees.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:16.520
Hey, when you went to get my present did you try to buy it with Takeuchi?

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:17.220
Yeah.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:19.890
Why did you lie and say you were going to an all-you-can-eat cake buffet with Mizu-chin?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.480
Lie...? I just wanted to surprise you.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.980
I know...

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:26.940
I know, but...

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.610
Don't lie to me if you're going to be meeting with another guy.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.610
I don't want any secrets between us.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.290
Promise me that you'll never ever betray me.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:38.830
Yeah.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.800
What page are we working on today?

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.130
Let me see!

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.800
Isn't it kinda harsh to be sitting next to Yamamoto-san?

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.890
She doesn't say anything.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.810
She scowled at me the other day.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.390
It's kinda hard to ask her to see her textbook, huh?

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.810
I hope they change seats soon.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.320
Let me see your textbook.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.900
It's hard to see from here, so could you put it between our desks?

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.620
Open to page 45.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:18.870
Ah, sorry.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.670
Why are you working ten pages ahead?

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.380
There's nothing else to do at home.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.720
There's nothing else to do, so you study?

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.720
You sure are different.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:17.550
I'd sure like some money right about now.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.390
You shouldn't talk about your unrealistic dreams.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.470
I have dreams!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.600
If I were rich, we could go on a date at Disney Land!

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:27.190
What about you, Yano? What would you do if you were rich?

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.150
Me?

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.900
I don't need money.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.610
I don't need any money, but instead... I want love.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:39.660
What's wrong with me, wishing to be rich?

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:43.290
Yano, don't worry! I'll give you as much love as you want!

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:43.870
Really?

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:44.960
Yeah!

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.620
Then, why don't you come over on Saturday? My parents won't be around.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:51.630
So love meant the perverted stuff to Yano...

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:57.220
Yano... in that case, want to come over my place on Saturday?

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.760
Huh? Your parents won't be around?

00:17:58.760 --> 00:17:59.680
They will.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:00.640
Then that's no good.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:03.930
Yano.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:04.680
Yes?

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.730
Is that all you think about?

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:08.350
Yes.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.150
You're such a moron.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:16.400
I'm sorry, Yano. I can't live up to your expectations.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.070
My heart hurts, too.

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:20.160
Ah, check it out!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.280
They look just like you, Takahashi.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:23.370
Should I give it a whirl?

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.290
Huh? I thought you were broke.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.620
This is my entire life's savings.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:27.460
Here we go.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.000
As long as Yano smiles back at me, that's all I need.
Here we go.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.210
Ah, that yellow one is cute.
As long as Yano smiles back at me, that's all I need.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:34.130
I should just put my other worries to rest.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:45.560
I want Yano... to always smile.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:50.400
Huh? I don't have my biology textbook.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.440
Even though I somehow managed to bring it home, I guess I forgot to bring it back.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.230
You're such a doofus. Want to borrow mine?

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.740
Ah... sure.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.450
No, never mind.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.160
On second thought...

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.160
Let me see yours, Yamamoto.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:15.920
Thank you.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.430
What is it?

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:28.100
N-Nothing! B-Bye bye!

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.440
What do I want...?

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.940
Yamamoto-san sure was nice, showing you her textbook.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.900
Ah... yeah.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.320
Yano, wanna come to my house on Sunday?

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.030
It should be convenient for you, since it's Sunday.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.990
Are your parents going to be out or something?

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.000
Yeah.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.540
Welcome!

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.550
H-Hello.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.510
It's kinda cramped in here, but...

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.880
You... knew from the very beginning, didn't you?

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.550
It's smaller than your room, but...

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:08.140
Oh. You can put your bag down over there.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:10.060
Yano's in my room!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.400
I'm... a little moved by it all.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.360
What is it?

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.070
Oh, nothing.

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.990
So, where do you live?

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:22.070
Yanagimachi.

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:24.160
It must've taken you a while to get here, then.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.200
Not at all. I just have to take one bus.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:28.240
You're so handsome. Your class must really talk about you.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.370
Ah, no... not at all.

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:35.460
Ah, geez... I'm starting to feel bad for Yano.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:39.090
I told you, he's involved with realty. Umm, Yano's house is really huge!

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:43.090
Really? And just when did you pay them a visit?

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:45.180
Crap!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:48.720
Takahashi, that house isn't as big as you think it is.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:52.770
You've never come in, but my room is only four and a half tatami mats.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:55.810
O-Oh? Is that so?

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.480
My. I see.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:03.950
S-Should I play a CD? What do you wanna listen to?

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:05.820
Anything's fine.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:10.370
I knew it... it's totally different from meeting with him outside.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.580
I'm so nervous!

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.290
Someone save me from this silence!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.420
I'm not gonna do anything, so calm down.

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:21.800
After all, it seems like your mom would just walk in without knocking.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.170
H-How rude!

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:24.930
She wouldn't do anything like that!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.680
Please have some more tea.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.270
Sorry.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:33.180
For what?

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:34.770
A lot of things.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:37.690
Don't worry about it. You're just being treated preciously.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.860
Yano, I really, really love you.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:50.660
I feel like I've learned so much more about you since we started dating!

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.410
Like?

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:55.160
Like? Like...

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:58.330
You can be a bigger doofus than I thought.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.170
Like your more childish aspects...

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:06.180
And how you brush my hair like this...

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:08.970
I just keep falling more and more in love with you.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:14.730
I'm jealous of Yamamoto-san.

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:18.150
Of Yamamoto-san, who knows more about the unknown Yano than me.

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:20.690
I want to be the closest one to Yano.

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:22.190
I want to know more and more about him.

00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:24.440
I want to know everything.

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:28.910
Is it selfish of me to want that? I wonder...

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:31.490
Yano, umm...

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:36.410
You said before that there'd be no secrets between us, right?

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:37.460
Yeah.

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:40.250
I'll never lie to you ever again.

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:42.540
So don't lie to me either, okay?

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:44.050
Yeah.

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:46.340
Would you tell me...

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:49.550
I'm sure it's all just in my head...

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:52.640
...what happened between you and Yamamoto-san in middle school?

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:56.230
Yano?

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:00.020
Why?

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:02.020
Why what?

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:03.770
For the same reason you have.

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:05.070
It's making me uneasy.

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:11.200
There aren't going to be any secrets between us, right?

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:12.280
Yano...

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:16.790
Yano?

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:25.340
Why won't you answer me?
